%I A323063 #23 Aug 29 2026 22:25:52
%S A323063 0,0,0,0,1,21,282,3102,30583,282368,2494567,21419586,180093792,
%T A323063 1493399792
%N A323063 Number of equivalence classes under rotations and reflections of n-step self-avoiding walks on the 5-dimensional hypercubic lattice that use all five coordinate axes and have no pair of nonconsecutive vertices that are adjacent in the lattice.
%C A323063 In the notation of Nemirovsky et al. (1992), a(n), the n-th term of the current sequence, is equal to p_{n,m}^{(l)} with m = 0 and l = 5.
%C A323063 For a possible interpretation of this sequence (in the context of a 5-dimensional hypercubic lattice), see the comments by Bert Dobbelaere for the sequence A038748 about a cubic lattice.
%C A323063 We have p_{n,0}^{(2)} = A038746(n), p_{n,0}^{(3)} = A038748(n), and p_{n,0}^{(4)} = A323037(n). For p_{n,0}^{(l)} for l = 6..10, see Table II (p. 1094) in the paper by Nemirovsky et al. (1992).
%C A323063 Previous name was: Coefficients arising in the enumeration of configurations of linear chains. - _Carlo Corti_, Aug 25 2026
%H A323063 M. E. Fisher and B. J. Hiley, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1063/1.1731729">Configuration and free energy of a polymer molecule with solvent interaction</a>, J. Chem. Phys., 34 (1961), 1253-1267.
%H A323063 A. M. Nemirovsky, K. F. Freed, T. Ishinabe, and J. F. Douglas, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1007/BF01049010">Marriage of exact enumeration and 1/d expansion methods: lattice model of dilute polymers</a>, J. Statist. Phys., 67 (1992), 1083-1108; see Eq. 5 (p. 1090).
%F A323063 a(n) = (A038726(n) - 10 - 80*A038746(n) - 480*A038748(n) - 1920*A323037(n))/3840 for n >= 1. - _Carlo Corti_, Aug 25 2026
%Y A323063 Cf. A038726, A038729, A038746, A038748, A323037.
%K A323063 nonn,walk,more,changed
%O A323063 1,6
